    <string name="cmp_pantalla">Equipment display</string>
    <string name="label_desviacion">Deviation</string>
    <string name="veredicto_ok">✓ WITHIN TOLERANCE — the compared value matches the reference (±%1$s%%).</string>
    <string name="veredicto_warn">⚠ MODERATE DEVIATION — check calibration. Exceeds ±%1$s%% but does not double it.</string>
    <string name="veredicto_bad">✗ OUT OF TOLERANCE — the equipment does NOT deliver what it shows. Requires survey/recalibration.</string>
    <string name="veredicto_sin_datos">Missing data: complete the measurements in this tab (and the calculators if comparing against theoretical values).</string>
    <string name="msg_falta_teorico_hormigon">No theoretical flow rate saved. Calculate it in the Flow Rate tab and press "Use this flow rate".</string>
    <string name="msg_falta_teorico_aditivo">No theoretical additive flow saved. Calculate it in the Additive tab and press "Use these results".</string>
    <string name="hint_aditivo_bajo">If the additive pump delivers less than indicated, check peristaltic hose wear, line pressure, and the RPM vs flow curve.</string>
    <string name="didactico_hormigon">Actual flow rate = 3600 × volume ÷ time\n= 3600 × %1$s m3 ÷ %2$s s = %3$s m3/hr\n\n3600 is the number of seconds in an hour: if you filled %1$s m3 in %2$s s, this is what you would pump in one hour.</string>
    <string name="didactico_conversor">Mass = flow × density = %1$s L/min × %2$s kg/L = %3$s kg/min\nPer second = %3$s ÷ 60 = %4$s kg/s\n\nDensity converts volume into mass: 1 liter of additive at %2$s g/cm3 weighs %2$s kg.</string>
    <string name="didactico_probeta_volumen">Actual flow = volume × 60 ÷ time\n= %1$s L × 60 ÷ %2$s s = %3$s L/min\n\nIt is normalized to one minute to compare directly with the display and the theoretical value.</string>
    <string name="didactico_probeta_peso">Volume = mass ÷ density = %1$s kg ÷ %2$s = %3$s L\nActual flow = %3$s L × 60 ÷ %4$s s = %5$s L/min\n\nThe scale measures mass; dividing by density converts it back to liters.</string>
    <string name="didactico_veredicto">Deviation = (compared − reference) ÷ reference × 100\n= (%1$s − %2$s) ÷ %2$s × 100 = %3$s%%\n\nPositive: the compared value is above the reference. Negative: it delivers less than it says.</string>

